  "parentCard": {
    "title": "Sprout's second showcase, produced by an older sibling, or a grown-up",
    "minutes": 15,
    "includes": "read-aloud",
    "steps": [
      "The older sibling or grown-up sets the room before anybody sits down: the family in a row as a real audience, a spot on the floor where the star stands so everyone can see them, their cup with the sprout in it on the table, and their toys counted out and waiting.",
      "Act one, the counting. They count ten things into a cup and say ten when the cup is full, then count the extras on top and say the whole thing as a ten and some more. They count, at their own speed, and a wobble in the middle is part of the act.",
      "Act two, the story. Five toys on the mat, two of them go away, and they tell the family how many are left and how they know. Ask how they know, then wait, however long the waiting takes.",
      "Act three, the pattern. They clap their longest pattern, and the whole family claps it back to them once.",
      "Act four, the seed. They bring the cup from planting week, show the family what grew, and say one thing the seed needed. The older sibling or grown-up closes the show by reading a book aloud to them in front of everybody."
    ],
    "notice": [
      "Do they say the teen number as a ten and some more, or as one word they have learned by heart?",
      "When the two toys go away, do they count what is left from one, or do they already know?",
      "Who do they look at when the family claps their pattern back to them?"
    ]
  }
